From b80e206d4de6678797c13f1ec4d7cb8b5f5f7922 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 20:16:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] core/output: never let an output mirror itself

OutputConfigurationV2Interface::kde_output_configuration_v2_apply() rejects any
client config that sets an output's replicationSource to its own uuid ("%1
cannot mirror itself"). That guard only covers configs coming in over the
protocol, but the invalid state is also reachable internally.

When two displays share the same EDID and have each been connected to more than
one connector over time, OutputConfigurationStore matches a display to a stored
output state by EDID hash and assigns it that state's uuid. After a hotplug
(e.g. a dock power-cycle) a display can be re-matched to a uuid that a still
present, previously valid replicationSource points at. The mirror relationship
that was legal when it was stored (source uuid != own uuid) silently becomes a
self-reference once the uuid is reassigned.

Because applyChanges() commits this directly to the BackendOutput, it never
passes through the apply guard. The output is then reported to clients as
mirroring itself, and every subsequent client config that echoes the state back
is rejected, leaving the output permanently un-configurable until the stored
config is wiped. This reproduces reliably with dual-head DisplayLink docks
(identical EDIDs, connectors swap on re-enumeration).

Enforce the invariant at the single point where output state is applied: if the
resulting replicationSource equals the output's own uuid, drop it so the output
falls back to a normal (non-mirrored) configuration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/core/backendoutput.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/backendoutput.cpp b/src/core/backendoutput.cpp
index 1bca7fdd71..dc929567fa 100644
--- a/src/core/backendoutput.cpp
+++ b/src/core/backendoutput.cpp
@@ -355,6 +355,15 @@ void BackendOutput::applyChanges(const OutputConfiguration &config)
     next.desiredMode = props->desiredMode.value_or(m_state.desiredMode);
     next.uuid = props->uuid.value_or(m_state.uuid);
     next.replicationSource = props->replicationSource.value_or(m_state.replicationSource);
+    // An output can never mirror itself. This invalid state is reachable without going
+    // through the kde_output_configuration_v2 apply guard: when two displays with the same
+    // EDID have been used on multiple connectors, a hotplug can re-match a display to its
+    // historical uuid which then equals a previously-stored replicationSource, turning a
+    // once-valid mirror into a self-reference. Drop it so the output stays usable (otherwise
+    // every later client config that echoes it back is rejected as "cannot mirror itself").
+    if (next.replicationSource == next.uuid) {
+        next.replicationSource.clear();
+    }
     next.priority = props->priority.value_or(m_state.priority);
     next.deviceOffset = props->deviceOffset.value_or(m_state.deviceOffset);
 
